fix(restart): relaunch the app restart.sh killed, not via startup.sh

The first revision put the relaunch in src/startup.sh, where
tests/startup-headless.test.sh failed it -- correctly. That guard states the
contract: desktop UI process management belongs to separately invoked product
entry points, never the open-source core startup. I had read the red check as a
stale flake and re-ran it; it failed identically, which is what a grep-based
architectural guard does and what a transient one does not.

Moved to restart.sh, before its terminal `exec bash startup.sh` -- symmetric
with the pkill at line 73 that creates the gap, and it leaves startup.sh
headless. Test retargeted and renamed to match.

Control: reverting src/restart.sh alone, keeping the tests, fails 3 and errors
2 of 7. tests/startup-headless.test.sh now passes 5/5 where it previously
failed this branch.

Stand: Echo Act IV Mini
